  "description": "NORVUN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H80 Gd8 N12 O44 4+,4(H2 O1),4(Cl1 O4 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.801-3.839 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.95-108.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ3-OH)4(nic)6(H2O)6]2(ClO4)4·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
